<article class="env-definition" id="0FXD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FXD">Definition <span data-tag="0FXD">13.40.9</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{D}$ be a triangulated category. A <em>right admissible</em> subcategory of $\mathcal{D}$ is a strictly full triangulated subcategory satisfying the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/0CQS" data-tag="0CQS">13.40.7</a>. A <em>left admissible</em> subcategory of $\mathcal{D}$ is a strictly full triangulated subcategory satisfying the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/0CQT" data-tag="0CQT">13.40.8</a>. A <em>two-sided admissible</em> subcategory is one which is both right and left admissible. </p>
</article>